 "text": "Okay, if you just bought Carpe or you're about to, watch this first. When it's new, it looks empty. It's not. Just keep twisting. It takes a bunch of turns the first time, and you need way less than you think, like a pea. Too much is how you get that white crusty stuff people post about. Put it on dry skin at night and let it dry before your shirt goes on, then again in the morning. The label says all-day fresh, and it's clinically tested for up to a hundred hours. But that's when you use it like this. This one's Mountain Breeze. There are other scents too. It's linked below.",
